    {
      "calls": [
        {
          "ID": "toolu_016vtNWpAtP8mkbTN2wLjVBa",
          "Name": "submit_read",
          "Input": {
            "assessments": [
              {
                "facts": [
                  "F1",
                  "F4",
                  "F6",
                  "S3:F16",
                  "S3:F38",
                  "S2:F33",
                  "S2:F34",
                  "S2:F40",
                  "F35"
                ],
                "ref": "N1",
                "statement": "The UK has responded to the US-Russia agreement by backing the US-led peace effort while tightening pressure on Russia's energy revenues and speeding up air-defence deliveries to Ukraine, not by easing off.",
                "supersedes": ""
              },
              {
                "facts": [
                  "S1:F12",
                  "S1:F13",
                  "F41"
                ],
                "ref": "N2",
                "statement": "The reciprocal energy ceasefire had not taken effect by 13 October: Ukraine was waiting for a start date to be confirmed, and Russia was still striking Kyiv and its energy infrastructure.",
                "supersedes": ""
              },
              {
                "facts": [
                  "S16:F72",
                  "S16:F73",
                  "S16:F86",
                  "S16:F93",
                  "F74",
                  "S17:F82"
                ],
                "ref": "N3",
                "statement": "Burnham's offer to Holyrood is built from tools for regional, localised delivery (No10 North, devolved employment support) and is so far made up of UK intentions; the only concrete matching commitment from the Scottish Government in the Record is its £10 million for two defence technical colleges.",
                "supersedes": ""
              },
              {
                "facts": [
                  "S11:F51",
                  "S11:F58",
                  "S10:F50",
                  "S14:F56",
                  "F70",
                  "S16:F86"
                ],
                "ref": "N4",
                "statement": "The week's railway and Scotland announcements share a focus on youth employment and jobs outside London: rail apprenticeships inside a £2.5 billion youth package, the GBR headquarters and a £1 billion train order both placed in Derby, and employment support offered for devolution to Scotland.",
                "supersedes": ""
              }
            ],
            "statements": [
              {
                "cites": [
                  "L1"
                ],
                "text": "Some background for the week: Andy Burnham has been Prime Minister since 20 July 2026. Until June he was Mayor of Greater Manchester, a post he held from 2017."
              },
              {
                "cites": [
                  "F1",
                  "F4",
                  "F6",
                  "S1:F12"
                ],
                "text": "The Ukraine announcements came after the UK's 9 October response to a US-Russia agreement. In it the government backed US-led peace efforts and said it would keep up sanctions pressure on Russia. Then on 11 October President Trump announced a reciprocal energy ceasefire."
              },
              {
                "cites": [
                  "S3:F16",
                  "S3:F38",
                  "S2:F33",
                  "S2:F34",
                  "S2:F40",
                  "F35",
                  "N1"
                ],
                "text": "The UK then went further. Its new sanctions package covers over 90% of Russia's oil-producing capacity, and it plans a maritime services ban on Russian LNG. It is also speeding up part of a £45 million surface-to-air missile package, on top of £1.6 billion for more than 5,000 LMMs. In other words, London is backing the peace effort while tightening the squeeze on Russia's energy income."
              },
              {
                "cites": [
                  "S1:F13",
                  "F41",
                  "N2"
                ],
                "text": "The ceasefire itself had not taken hold. On 12 October Ukraine was still waiting for a start date, and on 13 October Russia was still bombarding Kyiv and its energy infrastructure. Much of the UK's help is air defence for the winter, which suggests it is not counting on the truce lasting."
              },
              {
                "cites": [
                  "S16:F72",
                  "S16:F73",
                  "S16:F86",
                  "S16:F93",
                  "L1",
                  "N3"
                ],
                "text": "At home, the offer to Holyrood reads like a former metro mayor's approach. It relies on No10 North, the Scotland Office and devolving DWP employment support as 'a model of localised employment support'. On the UK side, almost all of it is still intention."
              },
              {
                "cites": [
                  "S17:F82",
                  "S20:F91",
                  "S16:F83"
                ],
                "text": "So far the Scottish Government has made one concrete commitment: matching the UK's £10 million for two defence technical colleges. It has also announced its own long-term local government reform programme. The next test is the National Economic Council's meeting with the devolved First Ministers, due in a couple of weeks."
              },
              {
                "cites": [
                  "S11:F51",
                  "S11:F58",
                  "S10:F50",
                  "S14:F56",
                  "F70",
                  "N4"
                ],
                "text": "Rail and Scotland share a thread too. Up to 600 rail apprentices sit within a £2.5 billion youth employment package, and Burnham met young people in Lanarkshire. Derby gets both the GBR headquarters and a £1 billion northern train fleet at Alstom's site there."
              }
            ],
            "stories": []
          }
        }
      ],
