                  "text": "The ceasefire itself had not taken hold. On 12 October Ukraine was still waiting for a start date, and on 13 October Russia was still bombarding Kyiv and its energy infrastructure. Much of the UK's help is air defence for the winter, which suggests it is not counting on the truce lasting."
                },
                {
                  "cites": [
                    "S16:F72",
                    "S16:F73",
                    "S16:F86",
                    "S16:F93",
                    "L1",
                    "N3"
                  ],
                  "text": "At home, the offer to Holyrood reads like a former metro mayor's approach. It relies on No10 North, the Scotland Office and devolving DWP employment support as 'a model of localised employment support'. On the UK side, almost all of it is still intention."
                },
                {
                  "cites": [
                    "S17:F82",
                    "S20:F91",
                    "S16:F83"
                  ],
                  "text": "So far the Scottish Government has made one concrete commitment: matching the UK's £10 million for two defence technical colleges. It has also announced its own long-term local government reform programme. The next test is the National Economic Council's meeting with the devolved First Ministers, due in a couple of weeks."
                },
                {
                  "cites": [
                    "S11:F51",
                    "S11:F58",
                    "S10:F50",
                    "S14:F56",
                    "F70",
                    "N4"
                  ],
                  "text": "Rail and Scotland share a thread too. Up to 600 rail apprentices sit within a £2.5 billion youth employment package, and Burnham met young people in Lanarkshire. Derby gets both the GBR headquarters and a £1 billion northern train fleet at Alstom's site there."
                }
              ],
